[00:37.16]Conversation One
[00:38.94]W: Good morning.
[00:40.01]M: Good morning. Come in please. How can I help you? 
[00:44.65]W: I want to know some information about your health center.
[00:48.05]M: OK. Actually, we have two health centers. 
[00:51.16]One is East Center and the other is West Center. 
[00:55.04]Both have a proper appointment system. 
[00:58.51]But because the East Center has more patients, its appointment system is more efficient than the West Center. 
[01:06.03]The East Center has modern facilities. 
[01:09.01]The West Center also has standard facilities, but it is not better than the East Center.
[01:15.94]W: OK. I'd like to know some information about doctors in both health centers.
[01:21.66]M: There are about twelve doctors at the East Center. 
[01:25.46]Among them, Dr. Sam is a really nice doctor who is good with children. 
[01:30.84]There are eight doctors at the West Center. 
[01:34.30]Dr.Jerry is one of the most famous doctors in both health centers. 
[01:39.59]It is said that Dr.Jerry is very good with leg trouble.
[01:43.51]W: Oh, I think the West Center is a good choice for me. 
[01:46.83]You know, I am worried about my son's leg. 
[01:49.56]M: By the way, if you want a doctor to visit you at home, you can reserve a home visit. 
[01:56.01]But we have a fixed home visit time. 
[01:59.34]Consulting hours for doctors at the East Center is from 9 am to 5 pm. 
[02:05.29]And for the West Center, the time is from 10 am to 5 pm. 
[02:10.66]However, if it's an emergency, you can phone at any time, night or day. 
[02:16.85]It might not be your doctor that comes through, though. 
[02:20.67]W: How about the charge?
[02:22.28]M: If you are a member, we will charge you eight pounds at the East Center. 
[02:27.64]But it is not the same fee with the West Center. 
[02:31.18]Because of distance, the charge will be nine pounds and fifty pence. 
[02:35.95]W: Sure. How about medication?
[02:38.66]M: When the doctor sees you, you will get a prescription. 
[02:42.19]You can take the medication you need at our health center or go to a drugstore. 
[02:47.19]If it's for a child under the age of 10, you don't have to pay for medication. 
[02:53.08]The same thing applies if you are a patient who is retired or pregnant.
[02:57.99]W: OK, I see. Thank you very much for your information. 
[03:01.88]M: You're welcome.
[03:04.42]Questions 1 to 4 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[03:09.76]1. What does the man say about the East Center?
[03:28.19]2. What does the man say about Dr. Jerry?
[03:44.41]3. What can you do if you want a doctor to see you at home?
[04:03.48]4. Who has to pay for the medication?
[04:21.02]Conversation Two
[04:22.90]M: Hello, Kate. How are you?
[04:25.04]W: Oh, fine, and you? 
[04:26.96]How did things go in the exams? 
[04:29.08]M: I'm not sure. 
[04:30.72]I haven't got all my results yet, but I'm so glad we're coming up to the end of the semester. 
[04:36.48]And I'm going camping with some friends. 
[04:39.11]What are you doing over the semester break, Kate? 
[04:42.18]W: I haven't got any plans yet. 
[04:44.31]I don't really have enough money to fly home. 
[04:47.11]I suppose I could get a part-time job and earn some money. 
[04:50.62]M: I thought about doing some summer courses, but I decided that's not a good idea. 
[04:56.29]I need a break. 
[04:58.18]Why don't you join us on the camping trip? 
[05:00.56]W: Well, I don't know really. 
[05:02.98]Would your friends mind?
[05:04.32]M: No, of course not. 
[05:06.54]They'd be happy to have you along. 
[05:08.94]We're going down to the Royal National Park. 
[05:11.95]It's about 30 kilometers south of Sydney. 
[05:15.09]We'll be getting an early train from Central to Waterfall. 
[05:19.15]It leaves Central at seven and goes to Waterfall via Sutherland. 
[05:24.06]Amin and Lucy are joining us there because they live in Caringbah. 
[05:29.01]Then, from Waterfall, we'll hike to where we're going to be spending the first few days. 
[05:34.91]That's at Garie Beach. 
[05:37.19]W: Where is the park?
[05:38.76]M: It's on the coast, but it's very big¡ªover 15,000 hectares. 
[05:43.84]We can hire boats, go boating and row boats. 
[05:47.49]There isn't much point in diving around there as there aren't any reefs or anything, so there's not much underwater life. 
[05:55.36]W: So do we have to carry all our food for a week?
[05:59.00]M: No. We've organized for the food to go down with a van, so we don't have to carry too much.
[06:05.60]You know Dave's van. 
[06:07.44]It's a camper with a fridge and cooking things, so we needn't bother with that. 
[06:12.51]But you'll need to bring your swimsuits because there are beaches, and the river. 
[06:17.36]You can swim in the river. 
[06:19.22]There are some beautiful little swimming holes with waterfalls in the river.
[06:23.73]W: OK, that's great. 
[06:25.40]I'm a bit eager to leave.
[06:27.78]Questions 5 to 8 are based on the conversation you have just heard.
[06:33.20]5. What does the man plan to do during the semester break?
[06:53.14]6. Where will the man and his friends go during the semester break?
[07:12.51]7. Which route will the man and his friends follow?
[07:30.64]8. What does the man suggest Kate bring?
