[10:57.77]11. Which place is located at the heart of the Peak District?
[11:16.22]Passage Two
[11:18.27]Each year, bad food sickens about one in six Americans.
[11:22.84]Proposed new rules aim to improve food safety.
[11:26.55]Officials say the changes could prevent more than one million cases of food-related illnesses each year.
[11:33.79]The new rules were proposed exactly two years after the Food Safety Modernization Act.
[11:39.84]The rules are the first step in putting the law into effect, making the biggest changes in food safety since the 1930s.
[11:47.92]The law makes the Food and Drug Administration responsible for preventing foodborne illnesses.
[11:53.81]Experts say this is a change from the role that the FDA has played in the past in reacting to disease outbreaks.
[12:01.73]Congress passed the law after a series of outbreaks linked to bagged spinach, peanut butter and other foods.
[12:09.83]The agency is proposing to require food manufacturers to show that they have identified where contamination is most likely to happen.
[12:18.60]Manufacturers would also have to show that they have taken steps to prevent it.
[12:23.45]The proposed rules also deal with safety in growing and harvesting fruits and vegetables.
[12:29.30]The Congressional Budget Office estimates that establishing all of the provisions of the law will cost the government $1.4 billion.
[12:38.23]But FDA Deputy Commissioner Michael Taylor says the new rules are worth the price.
[12:44.10]The FDA says about 15 percent of food eaten by Americans is imported, and that share is growing.
[12:51.32]Rules have not been released yet to require imported foods to meet the same standards as food produced in the United States.
[12:59.82]But the agency says they are coming soon.
[13:04.93]Questions 12 to 15 are based on the passage you have just heard.
[13:10.44]12.What could be the result of the new food safety rules?
[13:29.33]13.Who is responsible for preventing foodborne diseases?
[13:46.91]14.What should food manufacturers do to meet the requirement of the agency?
[14:06.52]15.What does the FDA intend to do in the next step?
